If you've a second SCSI disc in the box then  simply boot the CD once, get
to the menu, go to DCL commands, then MOU/FOR <disc_device:> (one of the two
SCSI discs) and then BACKUP <cd_device:>/IMAGE/NOALIAS <disc_device:>/INIT.

From there on your bootable kit is on real disc - way faster. I tend to add
all the other stuff I'd want to the kit disc at that point - LD, DFU,
ZIP/UNZIP and all the other tools you think you can't live without (see the
VMS freeware CDs or the VMS freeware on the web).

Have fun.

