Possibly because internet downloads are, at least to some extent,
generally traceable. The trace may not lead anywhere, but in many cases
it might.

If someone were to illegally run licensed software (via whatever hack),
and "borrowed" CDs, that would indeed be hard to trace.

If someone were to illegally run licensed software (via whatever hack),
and obtained the software via the internet, server logs (which could be
subpoenaed) may lead to the download destination, at least, if not the
location where the infraction(s) occur.

They'd just be trying to keep avenues open in an effort to protect their
IP.

