That's just plane dumb.  Every time someone goes to work, they are 
selling theirself, for the agreed upon time, for compensation.  Usually 
some skills are required to exist and be used during the 'work time'.

I personally don't see anything wrong with hiring someone for such a 
project.  What I do find distasteful is someone entering into such a 
contract, and then not complying with the terms.  Usually the up front 
money is already spent, and there is no way to recover the fees paid for 
the service.  That's just being a thief.


