Is it wrong to believe that everyone deserves the fruits of his own
labors?  Is that an "exaggerated obsession"?


> The idea of Stallman was/is to share common knowledge with others,

Share all the common knowledge you want.  If I do something innovative
it is not common knowledge.  If it were, it wouldn't have been innovative.
I can make it common knowledge, but I should not be compelled to do so.
That is just plain immoral.

> and that it's not a good idea to claim exclusive rights to ideas, algorithms, etc.

His opinion.  If I spent several years of my life developing an idea or
an algorithm that no one else was able to do up to that point in time
why should I not claim exclusive rights to it?  It was the fruits of
my labors, not anyone else's.

