> to people to learn from it or even improve it on their own is probably
> better than lame classroom or textbook examples.

Matter of opinion.  But some abstract "educational value" doesn't 
change the fact that it is the producer who should decide if his
work should be made public or not.

I wonder if anyone (even Stallman himself) remembers the incident that
actually led to his original tirade and the quagmire we have today.

