Well, yeah, that was my point.  If I understand correctly, the poster 
was talking about the CDs available from Montagar, and some of the 
products announced as available for download are not on those CDs. 
PAKs, yes, but media, no.

All that said, I think that HP has left this issue dangle, with the 
wording on the ConDist CDs from the past, and has not specified anything 
new for hobbyists.  Possibly it's just "not rocking the boat".  It does 
leave a lot of people feeling that things are incomplete.

Entering speculation mode, I think that Sue's questions in the last 
week, might in part have something to do with this issue.

The CDs that customers get as part of software maintenance may not be 
appropriate for hobbyists, due to there being products on them that are 
not part of those allowable for hobbyist use.  Therefore, the concept of 
just pressing more of those and making them available at low cost is not 
valid.  Designing and pressing CDs just for hobbyists would be an 
expenditure that just might not be viable.

One thing that I think HP could do is publish a list of products where 
media is available to hobbyists at some reasonable (to hobbyists) cost. 
  Allowing those products to be downloaded could be part of such a program.

I'm hoping a bit of patience will be rewarding.
