doub1eedge wrote:
> [snip]
> So - although I may die before VMS actually loads up (the drive is
> S-L-O-W) it seems to be working.  I'll ask ONE LAST QUESTION though -
> is there a FASTER CDROM drive I might get off eBay or other?  I'm the
> type who does 4 or 5 installs for practice and fun before finally
> leaving things alone, and don't HAVE this kind of time! ;)

Watch eBay for RRD43 and later (RRD44, RRD45). They're a bit faster.
RRD42 is a 2x(?) CD-ROM that uses the CD caddies. O.k., but you probably
want faster.

Also, some Toshiba 4x and better (non-DEC branded) narrow SCSI drives
can be jumpered to work with newer VMS (V7.2 and later) and they seem to
"play well" together.

