> >> house; there is a small mailbox here".  BICBW.]
>
> > I never saw a version early enough that it didn't start that way... but now
> > that you mention it, that bit does have a "tacked on" feeling to it.
>
> Hmm.  I've never heard of a version of Adventure (Crowther & Woods, whether
> augmented by Dave Long or not) that started with a mailbox--that's strictly
> ZORK/MADADV/Dungeon.  Adventure starts out outside a wellhouse.

You are correct.

I read that and thought he was making the point that if it started with the
house and mailbox it couldn't be Adventure, which is (or at least should be)
true.

I accepted that stance and went on to note that I thought the house/mailbox
seemed tacked on.

Sorry for not being entirely (or at all?) clear there.

But you got me to wondering if I was remembering any of this correctly, so I've
just started up the two versions of Adventure I've got here, and they both start
with "YOU ARE STANDING AT THE END OF A ROAD BEFORE A SMALL BRICK BUILDING,"
which is what I thought I'd see.

> In my opinion, if someone changed the original's beginning to look like Zork,
> they were serious losers.

Agreed.

> Then again, I hated the fact that Long eventually substituted a Wumpus for the
> Balrog.

I never saw a Wumpus in an Adventure or Zork I played.  Then again, I also don't
recall encountering the Balrog in either one.  But I always got lousy scores, so
I expect I just missed them.

    - Bill




