In comp.sys.dec Brian W Spoor <brian@fcs.eu.com> wrote:

[ Colossal Cave Advent(ure), not Zork|Dungeon ]

>A colleague (Richie are you still around) and myself spent many
>evenings converting/debugging and testing the Perq version - we
>found more bugs in the new F77 compiler with this program than
>with our "official" tests.

Widely available programs that stretch a language and/or its
implementation to its design limits are quite valuable.

Text adventures (hand-crufted parser, dynamic string handling,
interactive I/O) such as Advent are ideal to check Fortran and
Ansi C compilers and their converters/transformers.

A few years ago I surveyed various Fortran converters, and especially
with Advent I obtained some bizarre results.

At the moment I'm informally surveying the Intel 8.1 C++ and
Fortran compilers, and one of the programs I use is Advent.

scs


