> is there a FASTER CDROM drive I might get off eBay or other?  I'm the
> type who does 4 or 5 installs for practice and fun before finally
> leaving things alone, and don't HAVE this kind of time! ;)
>
> Thanks and Regards!

See my post on comp.os.vms to your question there.  The DEC RRD46 is a
12x CD-ROM which is a Toshiba XM-5701B with DEC firmware but either
will work. There is a jumper (5th from the left - marked parity but
apparently controls sector size) you need to have installed.  The same
goes for the RRD47 which is a 32x speed Toshiba XM-6201B.   Either
Toshiba is available on Ebay in the $10-20 range.  The RRD's are rarer
and naturally more expensive.  Be prepared though - booting form CD is
slow anyway on a PWS. ;-)



