I'm building a hobbyist DSSI cluster that consists of two VAX 4000-100A
systems. Each system has its own SCSI system disk and each system has a
second SCSI device. To create a real DSSI cluster I want to add DSSI
disks, one will be the common system disk.
So I got three RF31-EA and four RF71 disks. The disks were originally
installed in a DSSI expansion cabinet (BA400 IIRC) and came with a
frontpanel that includes a RUN switch and a DSSI unit plug. The disks
run fine but with the frontpanel in place. I know how to set the
unitnumber in the firmware and force the disk to use that instead of
the plug.
One question remains: how can you emulate the RUN switch on the disk?

Hans Vlems



