> ported to the PC that DEC never made and sold as a package.

DEC did actually make a "PC" that ran MS-DOS, CP/M86 and CP/M80 - the
dual CPU DEC Rainbow. But it wasn't IBM-compatible although you could get
third-party PC emulators for it (eg Code Blue) that created a mostly IBM-PC
compatible MS-DOS 3.0 environment under which most PC programs would run.

Andy






