In which case, YOU must already have copious notes on the game.  IIRC,
when I reported in to the "DEC Professional" magazine's stand at some
exhibition in 1981 that I had just that week managed to solve the
End-Game[1], they told me that I was "probably the 8th person in the UK
to have done so".

(DEC Professional were handing out a neat double-sided colour-printed A3
sheet of "the dungeon" which gave away all the secrets of the main game,
whilst still keeping the e/g hidden.  I've still got this somewhere,
along with my own maps and notes.)

So whereabouts did you get stuck?  I could probably find something to
provide you with a hint to get past the next stage.  Did you pick up the
Gold Card in the sliding block puzzle room?  That's one point that's easy
to miss.

[1] Which was an addition to the original, incorporated in the
VAX/MDL/Fortran version of Dungeon
