I'd find it surprising if the H11 had a Fortran compiler bundled in.
DEC's list price for an 11/23 with a pair of RL02s was around $25,000,
1980ish.   RT11 (or RSX) was bundled in that deal, but if you wanted
Fortran IV, then that was a layered product and cost another 1000.
IIRC, class "A" supported licence only.

Or did the H11 run a stand-alone .LDA binary compiled on a real PDP11?

