Hans Bachner wrote:

> Just for info - I have a 7305 (a "4100 in disguise") with only one power 
> supply, 2 CPUs, and 512 MB memory. When I got it I measured the actual 
> power consumption (with only 2 disks at that time) and it was something 
> between 350 and 400 watts.

The supply ratings are usually *very* generous.
I was told this was so that no matter how many peripherals and plugins 
you shove in it you could not possibly overload them.

A Vax 6000-440 which is (normally) 3 phase at around 3000 watts 
according to the data plate actually pulls about 2 amps from a 240vac
single phase common or garden wall outlet. The HSC70 is about the same 
and a block of 4 RA9x drives about 1 amp.
About 1200w for the lot.
The 5v supplies can deal out something like 350 Amps total - probably 
make a decent welder, so I wouldn't think the actual consumption will
get anywhere near maxed out.
I've yet to see an early Alpha box drag anything over 500w total.

-- 
The CO


