> The way I remember BA350 is that BA350 does have 50HD connectors at
> the backplane level. BA356 variants had on the other hand something
> called I/O module at same place and this I/O module brought the scsi
> connectors much closer for easiar access. With FAST WIDE style BA356
> one has at least two different I/O modules, one with 50HD connectors
> and another with 68HD connectors.

Pull the IO module and look into the shelf and see what the conectors
inside are: 2 Honda 50s, a 350 narrow, a EURO96, it is a 356 wide. A
356 shalf can have a wide OR a narrow IO module, so a 50 pin on the
module does not tell you what you have.

> The Ultrascsi style BA356 aka DS-BA356-xx (blue box) have typically
> 68VHDCI connectors on the I/O module

The dark blue is a bit of a clue as well!!

