group that had a contract with Corrections Canada.

As the story goes, a programmer was working on a tracking module and putting
the finishing touches on his code. The modules purpose was to keep track of
criminals that had been released into the community and their staus within
the Correctional system.

Apparently the programmer was supposed to using a Test System to verify his
code before release, but apparently he was also responsible for managing the
Production System.

So, in testing his code, he made an entry for a dangerous criminal having
just escaped from jail during a prisoner transfer, and proceeded to describe
a rather nefarious character. He then used his name and automobile
description and license plate, punched thet data in and was rewarded with
success, his code properly sent out the appropriate cross Canada notice to
various police departments.
Having finshed his test, he jumped in his car and headed home. Of course,
you can imagine what happened and on his way home, he was stopped by the
police and taken to jail. Apparently his boss was not able to come and get
him until the next day, and even then there were issues as the police were
finding it hard to belive htat these people were really who they said they
were, involved in creating and manaing the software for them.

The programmer of course had used the production system to run his test by
mistake.

rtt

Even if not true, it made for one hell of a funny story when I heard it.



