> In article <42ad3d77$0$52457$dbd49001@news.wanadoo.nl>, Alex van Denzel
> <vandenzel@hotmail.com> writes: 
> 
> 
>>>I'm trying to figure out if a BA35x (i.e. BA350 or BA356) is a BA350 or 
>>>a BA356, i.e. will it support wide (BA356) drives or not (BA350).  One 
>>>label says BA35x and the other says SWXCC-22.  Does anyone know  what 
>>>this is?  (I don't have it yet, so I can't test out anything.)
>>
>>Check the SCSI connectors on the BA35x. If they are 50pins its a narrow 
>>bus, if they are 68pins connectors, its a wide bus. I guess.
> 
> 
> The connectors on my BA350 and BA356 are all narrow.
> 

So your BA356  has a narrow I/O module now, the choices are

Module, 8 bit I/O Personality                               BA35X-MG
Module, 16 bit I/O Personality                              BA35X-MH

The -MG has two 50HD connectors whereas -MH has two 68HD connectors. 
BA356 itself is wide bus and the I/O module just brings either all of
it out (-MH) or the lower 8 bits (-MG)

_veli


