I did the port of Adventure to OS/8 that was available from DECUS. 
Getting it to fit on the -8 required me to compile it piecewise, then 
hand-optimize the pseudo-assembler output of the compiler for space 
savings. ("Piecewise" doesn't mean "by subroutine" as there were 
routines that were too large to compile as single modules.) The 
resulting tweaked code just fit in a maxed-out 32KW system. Any of the 
follow-on programs (Zork, Dungeon, etc.) wouldn't have fit even if you 
could have gotten them to compile.
