Hello, Phillip,

tomarsin2015@comcast.net wrote:
> Hello
> I am getting the following error when trying to install DWMOTIF on a
> 3100-85 with 64megs and VMS 7.3
>
> DEC VAXVMS DWMOTIF V1.2-6: DECwindows Motif
> @1988, 2000 Compaq Computer Corporation
> Compaq Computer Corporation
> This product uses the PAK: DW-MOTIF
> %PCSI-F-NOSLOT, no PCB available
> %PCSI-E-S_OPFAIL, operation failed
> %PCSIUI-E-ABORT, operation terminated due to an unrecoverable error
> condition

PRODUCT INSTALL needs to spawn a subprocess, but no more process slots
are available. Check the current value of the system parameter
MAXPROCESSCNT. Increase it by half or so, and enter the resulting value
into SYS$SYSTEM:MODPARAMS.DAT:

MIN_MAXPROCSSCNT = value

...then, run AUTOGEN from GETDATA through REBOOT:

$ @SYS$UPDATE:AUTOGEN GETDATA REBOOT

> Also the LAT service will start, but no LTA devices are created execpt
> LTA0.

Not sure what you're expecting here. LTA devices are created as needed
to service incoming connection requests, and are deleted when that
process logs out. LTA devices for outbound connections are set up by
the system manager as needed (usually for printers, but
"reverse-Telnet" has, for the most part, replaced "reverse-LAT").

Note that LAT is a proprietary, non-routable protocol - it is not a
TCP/IP packet sub-type. LAT does not traverse IP routers, it must be
bridged transparently at high priority.

> Thanks for any input
> phillip

Hope this helps

