This is a known hardware failure mode for RRD46 drives.  We have had
at least two fail the same way.  We replaced them with generic Toshiba
XM-5701B drives (an RRD46 minus the DEC firmware).  Because we wanted
our drives to all have DEC firmware, we removed the socketed ROM chips
from the broken drives and placed them in the generic Toshiba drives.


