No, it is not necessary for them to have DEC firmware (except possibly
for some older versions of VMS), however it is nice to have a recognizable
device type in the various controller and OS "show device" displays.
Not having DEC firmware could also cause problems with HP software
support if you ever have an OS software issue related to your CD or
other SCSI/IDE devices/controllers.  


