CI is/was the 80mbps full duplex thick cable ethernet used by HSCxx 
controllers to speak to computers.

So it *might* be a CI interface card (with losts of cache - though that 
seems like an awful lot of ram for something like that in that era), or 
perhaps more likely a 3rd party RAM card for an Alpha of some 
description?  94 is a bit late for it to be Vax.

