> > Any dramas installing a non RZ-xxx SCSI drive in an DEC 3000
> > AlphaServer?  Currently has some real RZ29B drives.  Any issues getting
> > some somewhat larger generic SCSI drives working in it?
>
> The hardest part will probably be finding larger generic SCSI drives with
> narrow interfaces, since the internal SCSI is narrow.

You can get adapters that allow you to connect a 50-pin narrow SCSI-2
deveice to a 68-pin wide-SCSI or Ultra-wide-SCSI bus - these connect the
narrow device to the lower 8 bits of the wide bus. Maybe it's possible you
get adapters that work the way round, attaching a 68-pin device to a 50
pin bus?

Andy






